h  stack already decided  um  slacking slack for communication github  git for code um  uh i would use for me i used r shiny and  stan  a little less shiny for this project but  it was still there um my teammate used  python javascript to build the web app  and so we split that way  it doesn't quite matter which you choose  to choose something that you're  comfortable in and can do something  quick  please don't ignore devops if you've all  been ignoring devops think hard  you want continuous integration you want  deployment and you want testing  even from the start you should think  about this before you enter  that way when you do something  you see the results immediately and as  you're going through this you can  iterate very fast and you don't have to  worry about oh how do i get this in  front of somebody that should all be  settled before you enter  um  for picking teams it's it's tricky um  you can go farther with others  but it's definitely harder to line when  you have more people  so think hard if you enter these  competitions who your teammate is  um and you cannot you absolutely cannot  micromanage um you have to split  responsibilities  if one teammate says they're gonna do  one thing  and that's not you  you have to let it go even if it fails  you just can't do it  so this makes actually choosing  teammates very hard this is why you end  up  arguing about what the problem is what  the solution is and what how to  implement  and the the last thing i want to tell  you is to focus so focus on the problem  the solution the implementation the  interactivity  keep communicating remember to keep  communication to the judges in mind and  remember to play the game  and then keep everything else out  if someone wants to argue about agile  processes like wrong team like that's  not for a hackathon sorry  um  all right and so if you're thinking  about entering hackathons are hard and  they are stressful  they're they're very very high variance  game because rules